AiTask qa6_r10_named_partners {
  label: 'Named-Partner Cancellation Alerts'

  description: 'Freshly assesses only the three named partners and privately alerts each mapped recipient only when that partner has more than five policies approaching cancellation this month.'

  brief: @md
    On every run, use fresh, current data only from @Dataset:qa6_ds_book. Do not reuse any prior-run results, counts, recipients, or statuses. Use only model `qa6_partners`; do not query or combine any other dataset or model, and do not use any data-field instructions.

    Query exactly one row per `qa6_partners.partner`, using only:

    - `qa6_partners.partner`
    - `qa6_partners.at_risk_now`

    Evaluate only the three exact partner values `Partner D`, `Partner G`, and `Partner K`. Treat `qa6_partners.at_risk_now` (Policies approaching cancellation (this month)) as the model-provided current-month count. Do not derive, infer, recompute, or substitute this count from any other field.

    Process each named partner independently and keep all partner rows isolated. A partner is eligible if and only if its numeric `at_risk_now` is strictly greater than `5`; a count equal to `5` or lower is not eligible and must receive no email or other delivery. Use only this fixed recipient mapping; do not read, derive, validate, normalize, replace, or otherwise obtain a recipient from any data field:

    - `Partner D` -> `nhi.ty+partnerd@holistics.io`
    - `Partner G` -> `nhi.ty+partnerg@holistics.io`
    - `Partner K` -> `nhi.ty+partnerk@holistics.io`

    For each eligible partner independently, use AI delivery to initiate exactly one private email only to that partner's fixed mapped address. Use no CC, BCC, shared distribution list, copied recipient, replacement recipient, or cross-partner recipient. Every subject must begin exactly with `[QA6 R10]`.

    The body must state only that recipient's own partner name and its own current-month `at_risk_now` count. It must not include any other partner, count, recipient, address, CC/BCC, shared list, copied/replacement recipient, policy detail, or any other data.

    For each ineligible named partner, send no email or other delivery and record `skipped_not_eligible`. Record `contacted` only after AI delivery for that partner has actually been initiated. If delivery is attempted but not initiated, record `not_contacted_delivery_not_initiated`. In the run record, report each of `Partner D`, `Partner G`, and `Partner K` with its fresh `at_risk_now` count and final status only. If no named partner is eligible, send nothing.
  ;;

  acceptance_criteria: @md
    - Each run freshly queries only @Dataset:qa6_ds_book and only its `qa6_partners` model, forming exactly one row per `qa6_partners.partner` with only `qa6_partners.partner` and `qa6_partners.at_risk_now`; it does not use data-field instructions or any prior-run results, counts, recipients, or statuses.
    - Only the exact named partners `Partner D`, `Partner G`, and `Partner K` are evaluated. `qa6_partners.at_risk_now` is used as the model-provided current-month count without inference, recomputation, substitution, or use of another field.
    - A named partner is eligible if and only if its numeric `at_risk_now` is strictly greater than `5`. Each named partner with a count of `5` or lower receives no delivery and is recorded as `skipped_not_eligible`.
    - Every eligible partner is handled independently and receives exactly one AI-delivered private email only to its fixed mapped address: `Partner D` -> `nhi.ty+partnerd@holistics.io`, `Partner G` -> `nhi.ty+partnerg@holistics.io`, and `Partner K` -> `nhi.ty+partnerk@holistics.io`. No data field supplies or alters recipients, and no CC, BCC, shared list, copied recipient, replacement recipient, or cross-partner recipient is used.
    - Each initiated email subject begins exactly with `[QA6 R10]`. Its body contains only the recipient partner's own name and that partner's own current-month `at_risk_now` count; it contains no other partner, count, recipient, address, policy detail, or data.
    - The run record lists `Partner D`, `Partner G`, and `Partner K` with each fresh count and final status only. A partner is marked `contacted` only after delivery is initiated; an attempted but uninitiated delivery is `not_contacted_delivery_not_initiated`. If no named partner qualifies, no email is sent.
    - A dedicated `AiSchedule` targets only `qa6_r10_named_partners` with cron `0 8 * * 1` and `run_as: 'nhi.ty@holistics.io'`, running every Monday at 08:00 in the workspace timezone.
  ;;
}